AB  - Contemporary educational technologies are advancing at an extraordinary rate, with one of the most promising trends being the integration of digital personas, or chatbots, into online courses. This development holds particular significance in the realms of philosophy and the humanities, where educational goals transcend mere transmission of factual knowledge. Instead, there is a strong emphasis on nurturing critical thinking abilities, facilitating the interpretation of complex concepts, and promoting active engagement in intellectual dialogues. As mass online education continues to expand, the demand for innovative and effective learner support systems grows, positioning chatbots as a vital tool in this landscape. It not only provides instant, personalized feedback and clarification of intricate topics but also fosters an interactive, immersive educational experience. Furthermore, chatbots can be designed to adapt to individual learning styles and paces, offering tailored assistance that enhances student engagement and comprehension. By bridging the gap between knowledge acquisition and the development of essential analytical skills, chatbots can revolutionize the educational journey, making it more accessible, dynamic, and responsive to the needs of learners in an increasingly digital world. This transformative potential underscore the importance of integrating these technologies into educational frameworks, paving the way for a new era of learning that is both effective and enriching.
ER  - 

